---
import CodeTabs from '../components/CodeTabs.astro';
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Introduction">
  <p>
    The Better Lyrics API serves syllable-synced lyrics for any song, for free.
    It powers the <a href="https://better-lyrics.boidu.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Better Lyrics</a> browser extension,
    and you can use it in your own apps too.
  </p>

  <h2>Base URL</h2>
  <p>Send every request to:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-bash">https://api.betterlyrics.org</code></pre>

  <h2>Quick start</h2>
  <p>Fetch lyrics for a song with a single GET request:</p>
  <CodeTabs tabs={[
    { language: 'curl', code: `curl "https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154"` },
    { language: 'javascript', code: `const res = await fetch("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154");
const { ttml } = await res.json();` },
    { language: 'python', code: `import requests

res = requests.get("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154")
ttml = res.json()["ttml"]` },
    { language: 'go', code: `package main

import (
	"fmt"
	"io"
	"net/http"
)

func main() {
	res, err := http.Get("https://api.betterlyrics.org/getLyrics?s=E85&a=Don%20Toliver&al=OCTANE&d=154")
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	defer res.Body.Close()

	body, err := io.ReadAll(res.Body)
	if err != nil {
		panic(err)
	}
	fmt.Println(string(body))
}` },
  ]} />

  <h3>Parameters</h3>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Parameter</th>
        <th>Required</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>s</code>, <code>song</code>, or <code>songName</code></td>
        <td>Always send</td>
        <td>The song title</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>a</code>, <code>artist</code>, or <code>artistName</code></td>
        <td>Always send</td>
        <td>The artist name</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>al</code>, <code>album</code>, or <code>albumName</code></td>
        <td>Always send</td>
        <td>The album name</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>d</code> or <code>duration</code></td>
        <td>Always send</td>
        <td>Track duration in whole seconds</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="note">
    The API rejects a request (<code>422</code>) only when both song and artist are missing. Send all four
    anyway: the cache key includes album and duration, so a request without them often misses the cached
    entry and, without an API key, returns <code>401</code>.
  </p>

  <h3>Response</h3>
  <p>A successful response contains TTML (Timed Text Markup Language) with syllable-level timing:</p>
  <pre><code class="language-json">{`{
  "ttml": "<?xml version=\\"1.0\\" encoding=\\"UTF-8\\"?>..."
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Key features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Free to use. Cached responses need no API key, and most use cases have no usage limits</li>
    <li>Syllable-level sync, with a start and end time for every syllable, for karaoke-style display</li>
    <li>Several providers: TTML (default), Kugou and QQ, each suited to different uses</li>
    <li>Heavy caching, so cache hits are free and need no API key</li>
    <li>Two-tier rate limiting that keeps serving cached responses under load, even to rate-limited clients</li>
    <li>A circuit breaker that protects the API from upstream failures</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Attribution</h2>
  <p>
    If your project uses this API, we'd appreciate a link to
    <a href="https://better-lyrics.boidu.dev" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Better Lyrics</a>.
    It helps other people find the project and keeps development going.
  </p>

  <h2>Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/authentication">Authentication</a>: API keys and when you need one</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/rate-limiting">Rate limiting</a>: how the two tiers work</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/response-format">Response format</a>: parse and use the TTML response</li>
    <li><a href="/playground">Playground</a>: try the API in your browser</li>
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>

